license: MIT
abstract: >-
  We provide an open-source, single-backbone, single-seed,
  fully reproducible benchmark of four post-hoc uncertainty
  quantification methods on the APTOS 2019 diabetic
  retinopathy grading task. The release evaluates plain
  softmax confidence, Temperature Scaling, MC Dropout (T=30)
  with four uncertainty signals including BALD mutual
  information, and Split Conformal Prediction (with APS
  variant). All methods reuse a single trained EfficientNet-B0
  checkpoint and a single locked random seed. Version 1.1.0
  introduces a novel methodological contribution: Ordinal-Aware
  Class-Conditional Selective Prediction (OACSP), which replaces
  the standard global confidence threshold with per-class
  thresholds calibrated either to operator-specified per-class
  target recall (equalized-recall variant) or to minimize
  ordinal-distance-weighted expected cost at a target overall
  coverage (ordinal-cost-weighted variant). At ~80% overall
  coverage on APTOS 2019, OACSP equalized-recall reduces
  Severe-DR abstention by 4.4x (44.8% to 10.3%) and
  Proliferative-DR abstention by 4.3x (29.5% to 6.8%) compared
  to a global confidence threshold; OACSP ordinal-cost-weighted
  achieves selective quadratic-weighted kappa 0.9218 vs 0.9068
  for the global baseline at the same coverage. External
  validation, multi-seed variance, Deep Ensembles, and
  Evidential Deep Learning are scoped for v1.2.0 and v2.0.0.
